  "content": {
    "id": "p47-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Consider $J=\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-x^2}}\\,dx$, with $x=2\\sin\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p47-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $J=\\displaystyle\\int 1\\,d\\theta$, and hence show $J=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)+C$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$J=\\displaystyle\\int 1\\,d\\theta=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)+C$.",
          "worked": "Choose $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}<\\theta<\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$, so $\\cos\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=2\\sin\\theta\\\\dx&=2\\cos\\theta\\,d\\theta\\\\\\sqrt{4-x^2}&=\\sqrt{4-4\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\&=2\\cos\\theta\\\\J&=\\int\\frac{1}{2\\cos\\theta}(2\\cos\\theta)\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\int 1\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\theta+C\\\\&=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 47
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q8-following",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p47-q8-instruction-paragraph",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Using a similar approach, find:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p47-q8-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{9+x^2}\\,dx$, $x=3\\tan\\theta$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac13\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{3}\\right)+C$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=3\\tan\\theta\\\\dx&=3\\sec^2\\theta\\,d\\theta\\\\9+x^2&=9\\sec^2\\theta\\\\\\int\\frac{1}{9+x^2}\\,dx&=\\int\\frac{1}{9\\sec^2\\theta}(3\\sec^2\\theta)\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\frac13\\int 1\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\frac{\\theta}{3}+C\\\\&=\\frac13\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 38
          },
          {
            "id": "p47-q8-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{3-x^2}}\\,dx$, $x=\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt3}\\right)+C$",
              "worked": "Choose $0<\\theta<\\pi$, so $\\sin\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta\\\\dx&=-\\sqrt3\\sin\\theta\\,d\\theta\\\\\\sqrt{3-x^2}&=\\sqrt{3-3\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\&=\\sqrt3\\sin\\theta\\\\\\int\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{3-x^2}}\\,dx&=\\int\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt3\\sin\\theta}(-\\sqrt3\\sin\\theta)\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\int 1\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\theta+C\\\\&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 44
          },
          {
            "id": "p47-q8-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4x^2}}\\,dx$, $x=\\dfrac12\\sin\\theta$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac12\\sin^{-1}(2x)+C$",
              "worked": "Choose $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}<\\theta<\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$, so $\\cos\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac12\\sin\\theta\\\\dx&=\\frac12\\cos\\theta\\,d\\theta\\\\\\sqrt{1-4x^2}&=\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\&=\\cos\\theta\\\\\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4x^2}}\\,dx&=\\int\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}\\left(\\frac12\\cos\\theta\\right)\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\frac12\\theta+C\\\\&=\\frac12\\sin^{-1}(2x)+C\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 42
          },
          {
            "id": "p47-q8-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{1}{1+16x^2}\\,dx$, $x=\\dfrac14\\tan\\theta$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac14\\tan^{-1}(4x)+C$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac14\\tan\\theta\\\\dx&=\\frac14\\sec^2\\theta\\,d\\theta\\\\1+16x^2&=\\sec^2\\theta\\\\\\int\\frac{1}{1+16x^2}\\,dx&=\\int\\frac{1}{\\sec^2\\theta}\\left(\\frac14\\sec^2\\theta\\right)\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\frac14\\theta+C\\\\&=\\frac14\\tan^{-1}(4x)+C\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 35
          },
          {
            "id": "p47-q8-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^3\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-x^2}}\\,dx$, $x=6\\sin\\theta$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=6\\sin\\theta\\\\dx&=6\\cos\\theta\\,d\\theta\\\\x=0&:\\quad\\theta=0\\\\x=3&:\\quad\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\\\sqrt{36-x^2}&=6\\cos\\theta\\end{aligned}$$\nHere $0\\leq\\theta\\leq\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$, so $\\cos\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^3\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-x^2}}\\,dx&=\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\frac{1}{6\\cos\\theta}(6\\cos\\theta)\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\int_0^{\\pi/6}1\\,d\\theta\\\\&=[\\theta]_0^{\\pi/6}\\\\&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 44
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
